The root cause is concrete: Lean calls `readlink("/proc/<getpid>/exe")`, but this audit sandbox’s PID namespace exposes only `/proc/self/exe`; the former returns `ENOENT`. I’m applying a narrow audit-local compatibility shim that retries only that failed `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookup as `/proc/self/exe`. This does not modify any frozen input or checker logic, and I’ll preserve both the diagnosis and rerun command.
